==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|wascan}}, {{m|goh|waskan}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*waskaną}}, ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*wed-||water; wet}}. Compare Low German {{m|nds|waschen}}, Dutch {{m|nl|wassen}}, English {{m|en|wash}}, West Frisian {{m|fy|waskje}}, Danish {{m|da|vaske}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈvaʃn̩]|[ˈvaʃən]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-waschen.ogg|audio|lang=de}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|class=6|wäscht|wusch|gewaschen|past subjunctive=wüsche}}

# to [[wash]]
#: '''''Wasch''' dir die Hände, bevor du [[zu Tisch gehen|zu Tisch gehst]].''

